<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        A dashboard is a screen of live widgets, such as a clock, who's working today, announcements or the laser
        scoreboard. Dashboards can be your home screen, and can also be shown on projection screens.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="Choosing your home screen">
        <FluentText>
            On <a href="/manage/dashboards">Dashboards</a>, select the home icon on a dashboard to make it your home
            screen. Select it again to go back to the standard home page. You can also choose under
            <strong>Home Screen</strong> on your <a href="/account/manage">account page</a>.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Everyone's home screen">
        <FluentText>
            Managers and Admins can use the people icon to make a dashboard <strong>Everyone's Home Screen</strong>.
            Anyone who has picked their own dashboard, or chosen the standard home page, keeps their choice.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Creating a dashboard">
        <FluentText>
            Select <strong>Create blank dashboard</strong>, give it a <strong>Name</strong> and optional
            <strong>Description</strong>, and select <strong>Create</strong>. Dashboards are shared across the company.
            Only Admins can open one to edit it.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
